\begin{note}
\emph{Quick select} is a variant of quick sort that returns only
the $k$-th smallest element of the input, indexed from 0.
It is commonly used in data science applications when trying to calculate the median or percentile of a dataset.

Because
we only need to recurse into the partition that contains the
$k$-th element, the recurrence is
\[
T(n) = T(n/2) + O(n),
\]
which gives $O(n)$ time in the average case despite quick select
sharing quick sort's $O(n^2)$ worst case.
\end{note}
